  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The agent correctly identified that `mapfile < <(gh ...)` discards gh's exit status so set -e never fires, and replaced it with `if ! out=$(gh ...)` so any non-zero exit (including one after partial output) fails the job while a genuinely empty org still takes the 'nothing to audit' path and exits 0, verified by stub-gh tests."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "Empty-org stays green, unexpected repos are still flagged, and the allowlist and workflow are untouched, but the agent also raised the limit from 500 to 1000, added a truncation check, and added an up-front allowlist-existence check, all of which go beyond the requested fix."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply names the actual mechanism (process substitution hides the discovery command's failure, so a 401 and an empty org both produce an empty array and exit 0), demonstrates it with a reproduction, and is honest about which tests do and do not prove the change."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 8.6
